# TerraDrift workflow

## Git

- Feature work: branch from `dev`, open PRs into **`dev`** (not `main`).
- Releases: promote `dev` → `main` when CI is green, then annotated `v*` tag on `main` per `docs/RELEASE.md`.
- Do not force-push shared branches or rewrite published release tags.

## Docs ownership

- Forward product intent: `docs/ROADMAP.md`
- Release policy: `docs/RELEASE.md`
- Packaging summary: `docs/GITHUB_PRODUCT_SETUP.md` (full checklist in `docs/archive/`)
- Completed engineering ledger: `docs/archive/PLAN-v0.1.md` (root `PLAN.md` is a stub only)
- Prefer editing these over inventing parallel process docs

## Safety

- No credentials, Terraform state, plan files, webhook URLs, or realistic secret-like fixtures in the repo
- Use synthetic placeholders only (e.g. `REDACTED_TEST_VALUE`, `https://example.test/hook`)
- Security issues → private advisory path in `SECURITY.md`, never public exploit write-ups

## Agents

- Follow root `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md`
- Always apply **Ponytail** (`.cursor/rules/ponytail.mdc`) — simplest solution that works
- Apply engineering quality + verify-before-done rules on every change
- Match existing Go and docs style; keep changes focused
